  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is zero information about baseline performance for any modality, encoder, or profile setting. The most critical uncertainty is the absolute performance scale of the primary modality (RNA) under the simplest, most standard configuration. 2) What this tests: config_001 (RNA-only, single profile, PCA-2000) establishes the simplest possible RNA baseline. It isolates the contribution of the RNA modality with a fast, well-understood linear representation and no aggregation or fusion complexity, giving a clean reference point against which all later RNA-encoder choices (scvi, scgpt), profile settings (multiprofile + aggregation), and multimodal fusion can be measured. 3) Why it is the best first experiment: Under a limited budget, the first run should be the fastest to execute and the most informative as a calibration anchor. PCA-2000 with a single profile is computationally cheap, minimizes confounding variables, and directly answers 'how well does the primary modality perform at baseline?'—information needed before investing in more expensive image or multimodal runs. It also serves as the control for every subsequent RNA-encoder comparison (configs 004, 007) and profile-setting comparison (configs 002, 003), making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice at this stage."
}

